WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:01.568 --> 00:00:02.702
IRIQTAQ HAILSTONE: We grew
up following our parents.

00:00:02.769 --> 00:00:04.904
My parents always took
us along with them.

00:00:04.971 --> 00:00:07.574
So I have that
mentality in my head

00:00:07.640 --> 00:00:10.143
that if I can't take
my kid then don't go.

00:00:13.446 --> 00:00:15.782
[peaceful music]

00:00:15.849 --> 00:00:18.017
CHIP HAILSTONE: He's
a handsome little boy.

00:00:18.084 --> 00:00:19.352
So cute.

00:00:19.419 --> 00:00:21.321
CHIP HAILSTONE: Wow,
you got green eyes, kid.

00:00:21.388 --> 00:00:25.825
My son's name is
Sebastian Orion [inaudible]

00:00:25.892 --> 00:00:27.360
[inaudible] Hailstone.

00:00:27.427 --> 00:00:30.430
Orion [inaudible]
is Orion the Hunter,

00:00:30.497 --> 00:00:31.898
so he's my little hunter.

00:00:31.965 --> 00:00:34.267
Yeah, he's totally
got your chin.

00:00:34.334 --> 00:00:35.702
It's the baby's name.

00:00:35.769 --> 00:00:37.170
Huh, Sebastian.

00:00:37.237 --> 00:00:38.605
Sebastian.

00:00:38.671 --> 00:00:40.940
I'm the auntie of 13.

00:00:41.007 --> 00:00:42.475
So I've had a lot of practice.

00:00:42.542 --> 00:00:44.778
Plus I helped grow up
my younger sisters.

00:00:44.844 --> 00:00:47.981
Now I have a lot of
help with my own son.

00:00:48.047 --> 00:00:50.350
[cold music]

00:00:51.885 --> 00:00:55.722
You gonna go ride with your
mom and go snares for rabbit?

00:00:55.789 --> 00:00:58.491
I'm going to get
the rabbits for you.

00:00:58.558 --> 00:00:59.993
Oh, you're going to
go get rabbit for me?

00:01:00.059 --> 00:01:02.162
Yes.

00:01:02.228 --> 00:01:04.597
NARRATOR: Mary's daughter Rose
and [inaudible] son Sebastian

00:01:04.664 --> 00:01:08.134
are the latest additions to
the growing Hailstone family.

00:01:08.201 --> 00:01:10.970
To provide her niece and
nephew with furs to keep warm

00:01:11.037 --> 00:01:13.072
through winter,
[inaudible] will head out

00:01:13.139 --> 00:01:15.742
to set snares for rabbit pelts.

00:01:15.809 --> 00:01:18.044
The task will also
pass on a native skill

00:01:18.111 --> 00:01:19.245
to her young son, Wade.

00:01:24.150 --> 00:01:27.520
In our culture, usually when
the women have a new baby,

00:01:27.587 --> 00:01:30.723
we try and make them
their own outfits.

00:01:30.790 --> 00:01:33.960
The best material for
our kind of conditions

00:01:34.027 --> 00:01:37.063
are the materials that
are locally resourced.

00:01:37.130 --> 00:01:40.834
So we're just trying to get some
rabbit skins together, and sew

00:01:40.900 --> 00:01:43.002
a few things for baby Orion.

00:01:47.173 --> 00:01:48.074
Oh, look.

00:01:48.141 --> 00:01:50.710
You see all the tracks?

00:01:50.777 --> 00:01:51.478
Wow.

00:01:54.080 --> 00:01:56.416
Yeah we'll get the
Willows first, yeah?

00:01:56.483 --> 00:01:58.918
So as we keep going we'll
be able to set traps.

00:02:05.091 --> 00:02:06.059
The rabbits are?

00:02:06.125 --> 00:02:06.860
Yeah.

00:02:06.926 --> 00:02:07.694
Wait, where?

00:02:07.760 --> 00:02:09.496
Over [inaudible]

00:02:09.562 --> 00:02:11.264
Wade just turned
three years old,

00:02:11.331 --> 00:02:14.234
so you could only keep
his attention for so long.

00:02:14.300 --> 00:02:16.903
He's a very active child.

00:02:16.970 --> 00:02:18.204
Watch out, Mom.

00:02:18.271 --> 00:02:20.306
I thought [inaudible]
your head, Mom.

00:02:20.373 --> 00:02:22.509
When we find something
he's interested in,

00:02:22.575 --> 00:02:24.577
it's entertaining
and fun to watch

00:02:24.644 --> 00:02:27.180
him because he's so involved.

00:02:27.247 --> 00:02:28.281
There you go.

00:02:28.348 --> 00:02:29.949
Some more.

00:02:30.016 --> 00:02:32.619
Oh, almost.

00:02:32.685 --> 00:02:34.754
I remember being a little
kid and following my dad

00:02:34.821 --> 00:02:37.056
out, checking traps and snares.

00:02:37.123 --> 00:02:39.025
You know, even though
he's at a young age,

00:02:39.092 --> 00:02:41.828
just watching and listening
to you, just being around you,

00:02:41.895 --> 00:02:44.364
they pick up and learn a lot.

00:02:44.430 --> 00:02:47.600
You explained things the
best you can, and show

00:02:47.667 --> 00:02:49.168
him what's safe and what isn't.

00:02:49.235 --> 00:02:51.638
OK, wait, I think we
got enough Willows.

00:02:51.704 --> 00:02:52.605
[grunts]

00:02:52.672 --> 00:02:53.973
You're going to
pile them up for me?

00:02:54.040 --> 00:02:55.041
Yeah.

00:02:55.108 --> 00:02:57.110
That way they're
learning how to provide

00:02:57.176 --> 00:03:00.079
and learning the cycle of
life and how things are done,

00:03:00.146 --> 00:03:02.015
and where food comes from.

00:03:02.081 --> 00:03:04.384
Thank you.

00:03:04.450 --> 00:03:06.152
OK, right there is fine.

00:03:06.219 --> 00:03:07.453
You could look in
the backpack and grab

00:03:07.520 --> 00:03:09.589
the snare wire, please--

00:03:09.656 --> 00:03:12.959
and the tool that's
in there with it.

00:03:13.026 --> 00:03:14.794
Here, Mom?

00:03:14.861 --> 00:03:16.429
Yup, I need that one.

00:03:16.496 --> 00:03:17.363
And where's the tool?

00:03:17.430 --> 00:03:18.798
I need the tool too.

00:03:18.865 --> 00:03:20.199
This one?

00:03:20.266 --> 00:03:21.167
Yup.

00:03:21.234 --> 00:03:21.935
Thank you.

00:03:29.075 --> 00:03:30.109
Sun's dropping on us?

00:03:30.176 --> 00:03:31.110
Yeah.

00:03:31.177 --> 00:03:32.412
The sun's trying
to go down on us.

00:03:32.478 --> 00:03:33.179
Oh.

00:03:36.082 --> 00:03:38.351
I taught my son
something, and it just--

00:03:38.418 --> 00:03:39.819
it feels good.

00:03:39.886 --> 00:03:42.088
It feels good to be
able to be that active

00:03:42.155 --> 00:03:44.357
and be able to do
such things up here,

00:03:44.424 --> 00:03:46.893
and teach my son that nothing
is ever too hard if you

00:03:46.960 --> 00:03:48.161
just set your mind to it.

00:03:48.227 --> 00:03:51.664
We'll come back tomorrow
and check our snares, OK?

